{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00360",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 3.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Good afternoon. Have a seat and we'll begin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.92,
      "end_seconds": 6.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Yeah, thanks. Sorry, I'm a little early."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 7.89,
      "end_seconds": 11.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.3,
      "end_seconds": 16.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit. You came on your own today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.23,
      "end_seconds": 20.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Yes, I managed on my own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.75,
      "end_seconds": 24.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "In your own words, what's happened?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.22,
      "end_seconds": 33.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "It's the room spinning. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.24,
      "end_seconds": 40.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Right, how long has this been going on? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.66,
      "end_seconds": 48.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "Well, for ten days, I'd say. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.18,
      "end_seconds": 52.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "What makes it worse, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.87,
      "end_seconds": 58.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Looking up and turning over in bed definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.98,
      "end_seconds": 62.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.44,
      "end_seconds": 83.5,
      "duration_seconds": 19.06,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get nausea as well. The nausea? That's been for ten days. About nausea, pretty mild, if I'm being honest. And I've been feeling unsteady as well. With feeling unsteady, I'd give it a five, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.86,
      "end_seconds": 86.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Any hearing loss, weakness or double vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.87,
      "end_seconds": 91.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "I, I haven't had hearing loss, weakness or double vision, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.03,
      "end_seconds": 94.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "What about numbness in the face?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.29,
      "end_seconds": 100.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Hmm, not at all, no numbness in the face."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.74,
      "end_seconds": 104.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.68,
      "end_seconds": 107.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.75,
      "end_seconds": 124.39,
      "duration_seconds": 15.64,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.2,
      "end_seconds": 127.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.79,
      "end_seconds": 135.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "Alright, do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.01,
      "end_seconds": 142.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for nearly five years. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.74,
      "end_seconds": 143.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.56,
      "end_seconds": 156.83,
      "duration_seconds": 12.27,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for two years now. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I've had arthritis in my knees for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.67,
      "end_seconds": 170.25,
      "duration_seconds": 12.58,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the high blood pressure in your file as well. Okay, arthritis in my knees, that's already on your record. Good to know. Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.67,
      "end_seconds": 173.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Not that I know, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.92,
      "end_seconds": 175.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.3,
      "end_seconds": 180.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.93,
      "end_seconds": 184.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.82,
      "end_seconds": 185.68,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.34,
      "end_seconds": 200.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.51,
      "end_seconds": 217.05,
      "duration_seconds": 14.54,
      "text": "I take telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day for my pressure. I took the morning off to come in today. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. Glycomet. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 218.45,
      "end_seconds": 222.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 1000 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.46,
      "end_seconds": 226.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.6,
      "end_seconds": 240.19,
      "duration_seconds": 12.59,
      "text": "Okay, so no, I left it at home. Yeah, I'm on paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed. I mean, I'm on Vertin, 16 milligrams, maybe, when it comes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.7,
      "end_seconds": 244.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.43,
      "end_seconds": 248.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.64,
      "end_seconds": 252.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.84,
      "end_seconds": 253.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.25,
      "end_seconds": 269.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 270.66,
      "end_seconds": 278.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Temperature is 36.6 degrees, heart rate 65, BP is 123 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.46,
      "end_seconds": 294.95,
      "duration_seconds": 16.49,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.46,
      "end_seconds": 298.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.57,
      "end_seconds": 302.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.62,
      "end_seconds": 305.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.29,
      "end_seconds": 319.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Your walking is steady and the finger-nose test is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.3,
      "end_seconds": 321.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.53,
      "end_seconds": 346.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "When I turn your head to the right, your eyes flick sideways, that's called nystagmus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.82,
      "end_seconds": 348.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.73,
      "end_seconds": 374.55,
      "duration_seconds": 20.82,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Putting it all together, this looks most like benign positional vertigo. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I'd also keep a migraine-related dizziness in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.9,
      "end_seconds": 386.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had the room spinning for ten days, and no double vision or hearing loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.11,
      "end_seconds": 389.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.17,
      "end_seconds": 413.9,
      "duration_seconds": 23.73,
      "text": "I'm going to order a hearing test, for tinnitus and vertigo. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Get up slowly from lying down and sit for a moment first. There's a simple head manoeuvre we can do, and I'll show you how to repeat it at home. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.4,
      "end_seconds": 428.17,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.56,
      "end_seconds": 429.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 430.7,
      "end_seconds": 447.9,
      "duration_seconds": 17.2,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you get weakness, slurred speech or a severe headache with the dizziness, call us the same day or go to emergency. Come back in three weeks. Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 449.43,
      "end_seconds": 453.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "So, I come back in three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 453.86,
      "end_seconds": 458.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "So, yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 459.21,
      "end_seconds": 463.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "So, you know, no, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 464.61,
      "end_seconds": 466.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}